Name: mutter
URL: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter
Version: 51.1
Revision: 9134e3a5869ce232bf95b77519005865747ba603
Update Mechanism: Autoroll
License: GPL-2.0
License File: src/COPYING
Shipped: no
Security Critical: no

Description:
A Wayland display server and X11 window manager and compositor library.

This is only used in tests.

Local Modifications:
None. src/ is a pristine upstream release.

The Chromium ui-controls Wayland protocol (used by interactive_ui_tests) is
implemented in chromium/meta-wayland-ui-controls.c, outside of src/. It is
built against mutter's private headers and hooked into the compositor by
wrapping meta_wayland_compositor_new() at link time
(-Wl,--wrap=meta_wayland_compositor_new in BUILD.gn).

Enum types, marshallers and D-Bus code are generated at build time with the
in-tree glib's code generators (see //third_party/glib/codegen.gni), using the
same arguments and inputs as upstream's meson.build files. Only the outputs
that need the host are checked in, under include/: config.h (from meson's host
configuration checks, as a template whose version is filled in at build time
from src/meson.build) and meta-default-modes.h (whose generator runs the
host's /usr/bin/cvt, from the xcvt package, to calculate VESA CVT display
mode timings).

This is updated by an autoroller that tracks upstream release tags. Point
releases only need a DEPS update. New major versions need manual work, so the
roll will fail; take over the roll CL and:
1. Update BUILD.gn to match the upstream meson.build files: sources, and the
   inputs and arguments of the glib_mkenums, glib_genmarshal and gdbus_codegen
   targets.
2. Run on_update.sh and check in the regenerated files under include/.
3. Make sure chromium/meta-wayland-ui-controls.c still builds against the new
   private headers.
